@@ -19,4 +19,4 @@ ISS-0014	2026-11-06	spec	Unconfirmed retrospective second-review findings (Kimi,
 ISS-0015	2026-11-06	ci	Sandboxes inherit the caller's git environment. scripts/checks/review_tool.sh isolated git config only, not the repository-locating variables; a pre-push hook of a LINKED worktree exports GIT_DIR=<repo>/.git/worktrees/<name>, so every git -C <sandbox> in the check acted on the caller. On 2026-11-06 `train.sh ci laudit` run from the linked worktree ~agent/audit-records made the hook's review_tool.sh create its test branches (nonff, capped, parse-*) and set core.bare=true in ~agent/audit-clone (kept unchanged as evidence), and push 28 commits to origin refs/notes/concrete-review (tip b4b364f4, pre-leak 5b6add0d) and 12 to refs/notes/concrete-review-findings (tip 21c56796, pre-leak fd3c6451), authored Review Gate, 17:16:49-17:17:43Z, annotating 21 sandbox commits that exist on no remote (first counted as 22, which wrongly included c54679c3, a real commit whose note at 17:21Z is legitimate); no earlier note was deleted or changed and every reader looks notes up by exact SHA, so none can count as provenance for a real commit. lambdaclass has no notes refs. Codex confirmed with a bounded reproducer on concrete-ci-2 at main f9a8c333 (caller refs and refs/notes/* changed: LEAK) and an independent GIT_DIR experiment. landing_script.sh and landing_bot.sh unset only five of git's local variables; legacy_frozen.sh, acceptance.sh, run-at-ref.sh and bot.sh unset none. Second incident, same cause: the first reproducer installed a pre-push hook that ran review_tool.sh; the leaked GIT_DIR made each nested push re-enter that hook, the recursion exhausted fede-256gb (load ~1900) and the OOM killer took down the orchestrator's session. Structural owner: the sandbox helper scripts/checks/lib/git_sandbox.sh (unsets every `git rev-parse --local-env-vars` variable), sourced by every repository-making script; reproducers and tests run with no installed hook, under timeout 120 and a 512-task / 8G systemd scope bound, or a finite cgroup memory.max plus a process limit, and never an unbounded run. Closed 2026-11-07: the fix landed at dbe838488891, where every closure part is checked in Root checks (scripts/checks/run.sh, all 11 pass: sandbox_isolation PASS=13 FAIL=0 with its structural leg over 9 scripts, the two live linked-worktree probes and the leaking control; landing_script PASS=208 FAIL=0 with the linked-worktree, hook-off, foreign-hook and identify refusal legs; also run on concrete-ci-2 at 8e62e377) (train siso from a full clone; reviewed by Codex, rounds clean at 8e62e377, and Kimi; CI run 42424663064; main CI 42425007584 on origin and 42425010605 on lambdaclass, both success). The stray notes were removed from origin by one forward fast-forward commit per ref on its then-current tip, no force: refs/notes/concrete-review d4bdcae22d50 -> dcffeea8e6cd (21 entries removed, 224 untouched at the push; Codex confirmed the list against the earlier tip 8cbb7db253f7, where 223 were untouched, and the one commit between that tip and d4bdcae22d50 only added a legitimate note for 9d6dc01a, so the removal list is identical) and refs/notes/concrete-review-findings 301e929e1bab -> 5d7c6dc3dad5 (11 removed, 105 untouched); the 40 leaked commits wrote 33 entries, one of which they removed themselves (0c04c01c); Codex confirmed the removal list and the tree diffs before the push; lambdaclass has no notes refs and none were created. ~agent/audit-clone is kept unchanged as evidence with LEAK-EVIDENCE-README.txt	R-0544	high	every repository-making script under scripts/ sources git_sandbox.sh (scripts/checks/sandbox_isolation.sh, structural leg); review_tool.sh and legacy_frozen.sh run from a linked worktree with GIT_DIR exported leave the caller's refs, refs/notes/*, core.bare and upstream unchanged while a leaking control is detected (same check, bounded); train.sh and the pre-push hook refuse a linked worktree and train.sh refuses a clone without the repository hook; and the stray notes are removed from origin by a forward fast-forward notes commit whose before and after tips are recorded here	closed
 ISS-0016	2026-11-07	ci	CI run 42424028055 (train legacydocs at 4d0355a56e, a docs-only change over 93850111) failed Kernel replay (leanchecker): the per-module leg replayed ConcreteSpec.Spec.Ownership, a module renamed to Slice1Ownership by 44ee1231, and stopped on unknown constant 'ConcreteSpec.lookupF'. The job's lake cache had been restored through a restore-key prefix from the cache of train commit 5b894432ad, whose sources predate the rename. Non-fresh `leanchecker ConcreteSpec` picks every .olean on the search path whose name has the prefix (the toolchain's LeanChecker.lean, lines 91-94), so orphaned build files are replayed. Reproducer: build 44ee1231^, build 93850111's sources over that build directory, run scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh: FAIL on the Checker/Syntax orphans; a clean build of the same sources passes. Codex confirmed it with that reproducer (2026-11-07). Structural cause: the replay took its module list from the build directory's contents instead of the sources.	scripts/proofs/kernel_replay.sh	high	closed by wip/replay-source-modules: kernel_replay.sh replays a staged library holding exactly the modules the sources declare and checks that the replayed set equals that list; scripts/proofs/lib.sh prunes build files of modules with no source before building; negative controls plant an orphan that fails an unfiltered replay and is ignored by the staged one	closed
 ISS-0019	2026-11-08	ci	scripts/land/train.sh review_provenance accepts a clean head review note without checking that its reviewed range covers the train diff; scripts/review/verify.sh:59 checks `base:` only as 40 hex, and train.sh:479 accepts the clean verdict. On wip/record-signoffs (head 0b9d3cfa3, clean note with base 1547734f8 = wip/record-language), a train of record-signoffs alone would have landed record-language's unreviewed content; record-language has no clean note and lands only by owner sign-off. Not exploited; nothing landed that way. Codex confirmed 2026-11-08 (VERDICT: CONFIRMED) using local bare repositories with no hooks: main A, unreviewed B, C on B, clean note on C based at B; review_provenance accepts C, while a findings note is refused. Structural cause: the note base is validated syntactically, never against the train base.	scripts/land/train.sh review_provenance	high	review_provenance accepts a head note only when the note's base is an ancestor-or-equal of the train's recorded base (origin/main at build), and a member note only when its base is an ancestor-or-equal of the train base; verify.sh takes an explicit --required-base; the landing tool's checks gain this reproducer as a control (clean note based on an unreviewed intermediate commit is refused; a note based at main passes)	open
-ISS-0029	2026-11-08	ci	At main ea212942 the decided R-0577 cross-machine comparison did not involve concrete-ci-2: reproducibility matrix extraction gave [('linux-first','ubuntu-24.04'),('linux-independent','ubuntu-24.04')], and compare-linux diffed only those GitHub-hosted manifests. Codex reproduced the defect by running the extracted comparison with identical GitHub manifests plus a differing concrete-ci-2 manifest: it exited 0 (concrete-ci-2 differs but is not read). Found by the retroactive full-access review of slice 0's landed rounds (86c31477..ea5181b5). Structural cause: the comparison consumed two GitHub-hosted results and had no concrete-ci-2 result. Structural owner: reproducibility/compare-linux in lean_action_ci.yml and scripts/checks/compiler/slice0_repro.sh. Fixed on wip/repro-ci2 with mandatory linux-github and linux-ci2 legs, runner provenance in each manifest, and a fail-closed cross-machine comparator	R-0577	medium	workflow_yaml.sh passes its structural assertions and exact comparison-step fixtures (identical GitHub/ci2 passes; differing ci2, two GitHub manifests, a missing manifest and missing hashes fail), scripts/checks/issues.sh passes, and a green branch CI run shows Reproducibility (linux-ci2) ran on concrete-ci-2 and Cross-machine reproducibility compared its manifest with the GitHub-hosted manifest	closed
