active full-access review of slice 0's landed rounds (86c31477..ea5181b5). Structural cause: the comparison consumed two GitHub-hosted results and had no concrete-ci-2 result. Structural owner: reproducibility/compare-linux in lean_action_ci.yml and scripts/checks/compiler/slice0_repro.sh. Fixed on wip/repro-ci2 with mandatory linux-github and linux-ci2 legs, runner provenance in each manifest, and a fail-closed cross-machine comparator	R-0577	medium	workflow_yaml.sh passes its structural assertions (linux-ci2 cannot select self-hosted on pull_request and its first step refuses a non-self-hosted substitute) and exact comparison-step fixtures (identical GitHub/ci2 passes; differing ci2, a ci2 runner_name outside ^concrete-ci-2-gha[0-9]+$, ci2 runner_environment=github-hosted, a missing manifest and missing hashes fail), scripts/checks/issues.sh passes, and a green push or workflow_dispatch CI run shows Reproducibility (linux-ci2) ran on concrete-ci-2 and Cross-machine reproducibility compared its manifest with the GitHub-hosted manifest; pull_request linux-ci2 is red by design before checkout	closed
diff --git a/changelog.d/2026-11-08-repro-ci2.md b/changelog.d/2026-11-08-repro-ci2.md
index 83a8356ab..52e69b471 100644
--- a/changelog.d/2026-11-08-repro-ci2.md
+++ b/changelog.d/2026-11-08-repro-ci2.md
@@ -1,9 +1,11 @@
 ### Cross-machine reproducibility includes concrete-ci-2 (ISS-0029) (2026-11-08)
 
 The required Linux reproducibility legs are now `linux-github` on GitHub-hosted `ubuntu-24.04` and
-`linux-ci2` on the self-hosted `concrete` runner pool, with no GitHub-hosted fallback for the latter.
-Each manifest records its runner environment, host and runner name. `compare-linux` verifies that it
-has one GitHub-hosted and one concrete-ci-2 manifest, then compares all build-identity and artifact
-SHA-256 lines. Missing manifests or hashes, wrong provenance and differing artifacts fail closed.
-The workflow check parses these requirements and runs the extracted comparison step against passing
-and failing fixture manifests.
+`linux-ci2` on self-hosted concrete-ci-2 for pushes to main and dispatch runs. On `pull_request`,
+`linux-ci2` selects a GitHub-hosted runner and fails in its first step rather than running PR code
+on concrete-ci-2 or passing on a substitute. Each manifest records the runner-reported environment
+and name; `compare-linux` requires GitHub-hosted provenance for one and self-hosted provenance with
+a `concrete-ci-2-gha<N>` name for the other, then compares all build-identity and artifact SHA-256
+lines. Missing manifests or hashes, wrong provenance and differing artifacts fail closed. The
+workflow check parses the runner guard and runs the extracted comparison step against passing and
+failing fixture manifests.
